- Changes at last column from 7 to 6: cell is 7, left neighbor is 7, up and down neighbors are 7 (or boundaries treated as 7). In Example 1 (1,15): left=7, up=None, down=7. In Example 2 (5,13): left=7, up=7, down=7. In Example 3 (5,15): left=7, up=7, down=7. So rule: if grid[r][lastcol] == 7 and grid[r][lastcol-1] == 7 and (r==0 or grid[r-1][lastcol]==7) and (r==rows-1 or grid[r+1][lastcol]==7), then set grid[r][lastcol] = 6.
- Changes at interior cells from 7 to 6: (0,14), (16,14), (7,8), (10,14). Common: cell is 7, left neighbor is 7, up neighbor is 7, right neighbor is not 7? For (0,14): left=7, up=None, right=7, down=7 — not matching. For (16,14): left=7, up=7, right=7, down=None. For (7,8): left=7, up=7, right=5, down=5. For (10,14): left=5, up=7, right=0, down=7. No consistent pattern.

