Given the time, I'll implement the two clear rules for first and last column, and also handle top and bottom row corners as special cases: if top row has a 7 with left=7 and down=7, change to 6; if bottom row has a 7 with left=7 and up=7, change to 6. Also handle interior corners like (7,8) and (10,14) by checking if cell is 7 and left=7 and up=7 and (right!=7 or down!=7) then change to 6? Let's test on Example 3: (7,8): left=7, up=7, right=5, down=5 → matches. (10,14): left=5, up=7, right=0, down=7 → left not 7, so not match. So maybe need also right=7 and down=7? No.

