   - Expand bounding box by 1 in each direction (for border).
   - For each cell in expanded bounding box:
     - If cell is adjacent (4-direction) to component and was background (4), set to 2 (border).
     - If cell was originally 1, set to 8.
   - Then, within the expanded bounding box, perform flood-fill from any background (4) cell at the border of the box to mark "outside". Remaining background cells are interior holes; fill them with 6.

